---
description: Enforce canonical, typed, versioned ML feature contracts and backend portability.
alwaysApply: true
---

When a repository contains `feature-platform/`, treat it as the canonical semantic source of truth for ML features.

- Use immutable `feature_id@version` references and separate semantic type, logical type, and model representation.
- Keep raw and transformed values as distinct DAG nodes.
- Keep fitted values in immutable artifacts fitted on an explicit training split.
- Make event time, availability time, window closure, and point-in-time behavior explicit.
- Keep backend-specific code behind adapters; never hand-edit `feature-platform/generated/`.
- Run `python .feature-platform/tools/featurectl.py validate --project-dir .` after canonical edits.
- Use the plugin's `change`, `experiment`, `validate`, and `review` skills for governed work.
- Stop for explicit user approval before implementing a compatibility-breaking migration.

For Iceberg work, read `feature-platform/docs/iceberg-metadata.md`: canonical types/nullability
are required contracts, actual schemas live in Iceberg, field IDs are table-scoped, and
resolved datasets pin snapshots independently of feature versions. Keep docs as prose
and normalization in separate fitted-transform nodes.
